jumpseat's OpenH264 v2.6.0 patch: screen mode's scroll search at camera mode's CPU.

Screen mode finds scrolled content by hashing an 8x8 sum at every pixel of
the reference frame, every frame: ~80% of its encode time.
- Run that search only on frames where scroll detection found a nonzero
  scroll, not on any busy frame (typing: 4.9 -> 0.85 ms a frame, +6% bits).
- Compute the sums from running column sums, ~4 ops a pixel instead of 64.
- Index every 8th column only. Scrolls move content vertically, so a
  block's match sits at its own x, which is always indexed. Scroll
  bitrate and PSNR unchanged; 5.35 -> 1.8 ms a frame (arm64, 1280x800).

